hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2893","**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us 'Abd al-A'la, narrated to us Yunus.

And narrated to us al-San'ani, narrated to us Yazid ibn Zuray', narrated to us Yunus.

And narrated to us Ziyad ibn Ayyub, narrated to us Isma'il—meaning ibn 'Ulayyah—narrated to us Yunus ibn 'Ubayd.

And narrated to us al-Dawraqi and Muhammad ibn Hisham, who both said: narrated to us Hushaym, informed us Yunus, informed me Ziyad ibn Jubayr, who said: I saw Ibn 'Umar approach a man who had made his camel kneel in Mina to slaughter it. So Ibn 'Umar said: ""Send it standing, tied up. This is the Sunnah of Muhammad (ﷺ).""

This is the narration of Ziyad ibn Ayyub."
"2894","Narrated to us 'Ali ibn Shu'ayb, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ishaq, narrated to us Wahb, narrated to us Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Anas (RA), who said:
""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered seven camels with his own hand while standing.""

Abu Bakr (RA) said:
""The narration of Anas (RA) is of the type which I have mentioned in other places in our books regarding the mention of a number which does not negate what is beyond that number. The statement of Anas (RA), 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered seven camels with his own hand,' does not mean that he did not slaughter more than seven camels with his own hand, for Jabir (RA) has informed us that he slaughtered sixty-three of his camels with his own hand.""

**CHAPTER:**"
